    "updated_at": "2022-06-20T23:28:44Z",
    "body": "I think #155 could also be tested, as with it actually being defined what it means to be an alias we can actually test _how_ they're aliased. But in general:\r\n\r\n1. People actually using the PR template (honestly just being explicit in the PR that there is no normative change is a win!),\r\n2. The editors ensuring normative changes having tests prior to merging them.\r\n\r\nAlso the whole UA string section is kinda unclear as to whether it should count as an addition per the working mode. Is it an informative section? Does it have any sort of normative status? Because it seems weird to have an entirely informative top-level section that… sorta defines things?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
